#: includes/admin.php:1250
msgid "My robots.txt is not delivered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1251
msgid "Check that there is no physical robots.txt in the web root and that the site is not set to \"Discourage search engines\". In a network, the overview shows the source and the status of every site. Override files must be readable by the web server."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1252
msgid "I changed the content in the editor, but the old one is still delivered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1253
msgid "A file in the override directory takes precedence over the database content. Delete the file – or copy it into the database first with the button in the editor. A page cache or CDN may also deliver an old copy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1254
msgid "What is the difference between \"Base\" and \"Exact\"?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1255
msgid "In \"Base\" mode, the content replaces the WordPress default and SEO plugins may still change it: Yoast SEO removes the WordPress default rules and appends its own rules and sitemap, All in One SEO rebuilds the robots.txt. In \"Exact\" mode, a custom robots.txt is delivered as is. The default mode is set in the settings; each site can choose its own in its editor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1256
msgid "What does the status check?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1257
msgid "It requests the robots.txt of the site as crawlers get it and shows whether all crawlers are blocked, how many sitemaps are linked and whether crawlers that collect content for AI training are blocked. The result is kept for the time set in the settings and can be checked again at any time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1258
msgid "Does it work if WordPress is installed in a subdirectory?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1259
msgid "If the address of the site contains a path (example.com/blog/), crawlers request the robots.txt from example.com/robots.txt, which WordPress does not deliver. The plugin then does nothing and says so. If only the WordPress files are in a subdirectory and the address is the root of the domain, it works."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1260
msgid "What happens on uninstall?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin.php:1261
msgid "The settings and everything stored in the database are deleted. Files in the override directory and a renamed _old-robots.txt are kept."
msgstr ""
